<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<metadata>
  <!--
    What is deliberately NOT bound.

    com.tidal.sdk.player.events.model is TIDAL's playback telemetry — the events the
    SDK sends home about what played, at what quality, over which CDM. Score never
    reads it, and it does not survive the trip into C#: the models are a Kotlin sealed
    hierarchy whose members narrow their inherited return types, which Java's generics
    can express and C#'s override rules cannot. Every one of the 25 errors the first
    build produced was in this one package.

    Removing it here takes it out of the generated C# only. The classes are still in
    the packaged .aar, so the SDK sends its telemetry at runtime exactly as its own
    terms require — this is a binding decision, not a modification of the player.
  -->
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='com.tidal.sdk.player.events.model']" />
</metadata>
